    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ποτνιαί</span></b> , αἱ, an
		ancient 
			Boeot.
		 town called after <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ
		Πότνιαι</span> (= Demeter and Kore), <i><span class="en">
			Paus.
			9.8.1
		</span></i>; conjectured to be the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑποθῆβαι</span> of Homer, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			9.2.32
		</span></i>: hence Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ποτνιεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Potnian,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γλαῦκος Π.</span> title of play by <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i></div>
